{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"9d6d75ac79715f19","name":"card_event_edge_of_the_empire","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/WorldAtWar/events/card_event_edge_of_the_empire","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"EDGE OF THE EMPIRE","text":"Shuffle your hand into your deck. Draw 3 cards at the end of turn.","flavorText":"The Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere, also known as the “New Order in East Asia”, was a concept where the idea was to liberate Asia from the Western colonial powers and create a bloc of Asian nations which would be led by Japan. This concept served as a front for Japan's expansion in Asia during WWII, but the controversy was that Japan replaced the Western powers with a ruthless administration and drained the resources in most of their conquered nations in order to achieve their own imperial ambitions. At the height of WWII, the Empire of Japan was one of the largest in history, its sovereignty reached 8,510,000 km2 and its occupied regions and territories population accounted for 20% of the world's population. However, following Japan’s surrender to the Allies in September 1945 its governance was restricted to Japan and its islands and as a result the Co-Prosperity Sphere ceased to exist.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_edge_of_the_empire","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_edge_of_the_empire_title","SourceString":"EDGE OF THE EMPIRE","LocalizedString":"EDGE OF THE EMPIRE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_edge_of_the_empire_text","SourceString":"Shuffle your hand into your deck. Draw 3 cards at the end of turn.","LocalizedString":"Shuffle your hand into your deck. Draw 3 cards at the end of turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_edge_of_the_empire_history","SourceString":"The Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere, also known as the “New Order in East Asia”, was a concept where the idea was to liberate Asia from the Western colonial powers and create a bloc of Asian nations which would be led by Japan. This concept served as a front for Japan's expansion in Asia during WWII, but the controversy was that Japan replaced the Western powers with a ruthless administration and drained the resources in most of their conquered nations in order to achieve their own imperial ambitions. At the height of WWII, the Empire of Japan was one of the largest in history, its sovereignty reached 8,510,000 km2 and its occupied regions and territories population accounted for 20% of the world's population. However, following Japan’s surrender to the Allies in September 1945 its governance was restricted to Japan and its islands and as a result the Co-Prosperity Sphere ceased to exist.","LocalizedString":"The Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere, also known as the “New Order in East Asia”, was a concept where the idea was to liberate Asia from the Western colonial powers and create a bloc of Asian nations which would be led by Japan. This concept served as a front for Japan's expansion in Asia during WWII, but the controversy was that Japan replaced the Western powers with a ruthless administration and drained the resources in most of their conquered nations in order to achieve their own imperial ambitions. At the height of WWII, the Empire of Japan was one of the largest in history, its sovereignty reached 8,510,000 km2 and its occupied regions and territories population accounted for 20% of the world's population. However, following Japan’s surrender to the Allies in September 1945 its governance was restricted to Japan and its islands and as a result the Co-Prosperity Sphere ceased to exist."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction